uh hey sandra just right around the  corner from john here and you know it  started on this trip  earlier this week with a g7 statement to  this effect pushing  on the w.h.o in covid19 we have just  gotten a statement  from the united states and european  union that had some consultations in  brussels saying quote  we call for progress on a transparent  evidence-based and expert-led who  convened phase 2 study  on the origins of covet 19 that is free  from interference  and we commit to working together  towards development and use of a swift  and independent means  for investigating such outbreaks in the  future china's government refuses that  an independent examination  into the origins of the virus in china  to determine whether this came from  nature  or the wuhan institute of virology and  with that  republican congressional leaders are  calling for another domestic  inquiry definitely not using the world  health organization to investigate why  don't you just ask china to investigate  it as well  hold china accountable for what they  have done and the deaths that they have  caused around the world  secretary of state anthony blinken who  was also on this trip with president  biden  called the world health organization's  first investigation  highly deficient and that there needs to  be accountability for china though it is  unclear what exactly that accountability  will be  and if the united states and biden  administration determine it  whether american allies will join the  u.s  in that accountability for now officials  are pointing to that  independent review that the u.s  intelligence committee is looking into  to look into whether this was a lab leak  or came from nature which is due by the  end  of august sandra all right good stuff  from there a change of scenery for you  as well rich edson thank you  john uh yeah he's experiencing  the same beautiful scene that we are  there's another scene there on capitol  hill let's bring in senator rand paul of  the great state of kentucky  so senator paul the w.h.o being  instructed by the g7 and we should point  out the who is headquartered here in  geneva  to undertake a second review of the  origins of covet 19 and whether or not  it came out of the laboratory  didn't einstein once say that the  definition of insanity is doing the same  thing over and over again  expecting a different result here's the  problem the who investigated this the  first time  we suggested three people to send to  china they rejected all three and they  accepted a guy named peter dezak  who was the one who funded the lab so  you can't have the people  like peter anthony fauci or peter dazak  who  who were part of the funding mechanism  to send these funds to wuhan lab  you can't have them investigating  themselves they have a  definite conflict of interest because if  if this  pandemic started a lab that the u.s was  funding  the people advocating for the funding  obviously will have  you know culpability at least moral  culpability so they can't be  investigating themselves  the who did a terrible job the first  time there needs to be investigation but  i've been advocating  for a congressional investigation in the  senate i've asked two committees that  i'm on  homeland security and the help committee  the health  labor and pensions committee to  investigate this i haven't heard back  from the democrat chairman so far  but i think this should be investigated  i don't think it has to be partisan  we should all want to know how this  pandemic started but we should all want  to know so we don't have this happen  again with another lab leak  of an even more dangerous virus  the the communique that came out of the  g7 summit in cornwall  england talked tough about china in  terms of wanting to get to the bottom of  coronavirus  had something to say about their human  rights abuses the chinese communist  party basically took a page out of  vladimir putin's playbook and said who  cares what a handful of nations say  we're looking toward the g20 summit uh  this fall  it's a much bigger group does the g7  have have they have to try to put the  screws to china particularly when  countries like germany are really you  know getting into bigger economic deals  with with china  where france is being invested into a  much greater degree i mean the chinese  bought club med for pizza  so do they have the half to be able to  put the screws to china  i think it's very difficult for any  international body to make another  country that doesn't want to listen  behave i do think though that the entire  world was affected by this pandemic over  three and a half million people have  died  the type of research that they're doing  in china has even deadlier implications  one of the viruses they've been working  on has a 15  mortality which would be 15 times  greater over  50 million people dead so yes the whole  world has a self-interest  in making sure that china behaves but  the only way we'll get them to behave is  with  ostracism by the whole world and i agree  with president trump we shouldn't have  been we should have gotten out of the  who and say we only get back in  you only get us money we only get any of  our money  if there's a real honest-to-goodness  investigation of where this virus came  from  let me get you to weigh in on tomorrow's  summit for a little bit if i could uh  when he was leaving nato  president biden suggesting that uh putin  is a worthy adversary dialing back his  criticisms just a little bit  also with a preview of tomorrow's summit  saying he's not looking for conflict  with russia  listen here then i'll get you to react  on the other side  i'm not looking for conflict with russia  but that we will respond if russia  continues its harmful activities  and we will not fail to defend the  transatlantic alliance  or stand up for democratic values  is dialing back the west best way to  deal with vladimir putin or should he go  into that meeting tomorrow with his  gloves off  you know i think we're approaching a  time period that's not uh too dissimilar  than the cold war  in the cold war you know russia the  soviet union had all kinds of human  rights abuses  we objected to it we spoke out against  it and yet reagan did at some point sit  down with gorbachev and talk about  nuclear arms control  i think we have the same sort of  scenario now you know there's great deal  of evidence of poisoning of their  opponents  of people being poisoned around the  world by a russian nerve agent which  you know seems to have come from russia  so the thing is is we have all those  things they all need to be condemned but  at the same time we still need to have  conversation with both russia and china  over nuclear arms control  we need to make sure that the world is  assured that we are not  a believer in the first strike of other  nations and that we are a civilized  nation that wants to reduce nuclear arms  i think those are important no matter  how bad the human rights  records are of other countries that we  continue to have some dialogue  give me just a couple of seconds of this  because we're just running short of time  here senator paul  should there be a joint press conference  tomorrow between the two leaders  should president biden get up there on  stage with putin and talk tough publicly  you know i think uh optics are important  and i don't know if i have the best  advice on whether it should be joint or  separate  but i think there are ways uh to make  our case known  to condemn human rights abuses but at  the same time still be willing to have a  dialogue with russia and china  so it's a difficult and delicate dance  diplomacy  but the main thing is we cannot cut  ourselves off we cannot  refuse to have dialogue we still need to  have open dialogue with both china and  russia  yeah you don't just talk to your allies  and talk to your adversaries as well  senator rand paul of kentucky thanks for  joining us appreciate it

